design-context-bridge (vendored subset)
=======================================

Source:   https://github.com/CristinaFores/design-context-bridge
License:  MIT (see LICENSE in this directory)
Vendored: commit 2e747e2
Scope:    src/core, src/figma-bridge, src/figma-rest, src/mcp-server/tools
          (src/index.ts and src/mcp-server/tool-registry.ts were removed; the
          tool surface is adapted in src/figma/ with zod input schemas).

Modifications (all files also carry inline PATCH notes):
  1. figma-bridge/store.ts      — temp-file prefix `aos-mcp-figma-` to avoid
                                   clashing with a stock installation.
  2. figma-bridge/ws-server.ts  — rewritten: CORS origin allowlist (null /
                                   loopback only), EADDRINUSE reports
                                   `skipped_occupied` instead of silent file
                                   sharing, startFigmaBridge() returns a status
                                   handle and accepts {port, host}.
  3. figma-rest/client.ts       — token guidance message now points at the
                                   project .env / aos_configure tool.
  4. figma-rest/analysis.ts     — rgbaToHex keeps #RRGGBBAA alpha (paint opacity
                                   multiplied into the color's own alpha) so
                                   translucent colors stay distinct during
                                   dedup/naming (M6a).
  5. figma-rest/client.ts       — rate-limit hardening: bounded Retry-After
                                   (AOS_FIGMA_RETRY_MAX_WAIT_MS, default 60s —
                                   longer lockouts fail fast instead of
                                   sleeping), per-token cooldown memory with
                                   fail-fast before any request, typed
                                   FigmaRateLimitError carrying tier
                                   (`x-figma-rate-limit-type`) and retry-after,
                                   response cache TTL raised to 10min and made
                                   configurable (AOS_FIGMA_CACHE_TTL_MS, 0
                                   disables).

Everything else is unmodified upstream code. The original MIT license and
copyright notices are preserved in LICENSE.
